---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import AppleIcon from '../components/AppleIcon.astro';
const date = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { dateStyle: 'long', timeZone: 'UTC' }).format(new Date(site.releaseDate));
---
<Layout title="Download Folio for Mac" description={`Download Folio ${site.version} for ${site.minMacOS} or later.`}>
  <section class="container-x max-w-3xl py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 !text-5xl sm:!text-6xl">Download <span translate="no">{site.name}</span> for&nbsp;Mac.</h1>
    <p class="lead mt-5">Version {site.version} · {date}.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row"><a href={site.downloadUrl} class="btn-primary"><AppleIcon />Download .dmg</a><a href={site.checkoutUrl} class="btn-secondary">Buy a License</a></div>
    <dl class="mt-12 divide-y divide-hairline rounded-md border border-hairline bg-elevated text-sm">
      {[['Requires', `${site.minMacOS} or later`], ['Price', `${site.price.label} per license (one Mac)`]].map(([k, v]) => (
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-mute">{k}</dt><dd class="text-ink">{v}</dd></div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2 id="install" class="h2 mt-16">How to install</h2>
    <p class="lead mt-3"><span translate="no">{site.name}</span> is not yet notarized by Apple, so macOS shows a warning the first time you open it. This is expected, and you only need to do the steps below once.</p>
    <ol class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-base leading-7">
      <li><strong class="text-ink">1. Open the download.</strong> Double-click the .dmg file, then drag <span translate="no">{site.name}</span> into your Applications folder.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">2. Try to open it.</strong> Launch <span translate="no">{site.name}</span> from Applications. macOS will say it cannot verify the app. Click <em>Done</em> (or <em>Cancel</em>).</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">3. Allow it in System Settings.</strong> Open <em>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</em>, scroll to the Security section, and click <em>Open Anyway</em> next to <span translate="no">{site.name}</span>. Enter your password if asked, then click <em>Open</em>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-6">On macOS 14 or earlier you can skip step 3: right-click (or Control-click) <span translate="no">{site.name}</span> in Applications, choose <em>Open</em>, then click <em>Open</em> again.</p>

    <h3 class="mt-10 text-xl tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Still blocked, or "app is damaged"?</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6">Quarantine flags added by the browser can cause this. Open Terminal and run the command below, then launch the app again.</p>
    <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-hairline bg-elevated px-4 py-3 text-sm"><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Folio.app</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-6">We are working on Apple notarization, after which these steps will no longer be needed.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
